So downSample uses `sampleValue(frame)` to compute a value, then `sampleIndex(frameValues, value)` computes which index within the frame to pick. The generic `indexSampler` returns `Math.round(frame.length / 2)` — the middle point. Then the sampled value is written to the dimStore at that index.

For `minmax` mode, the value is the point with max absolute value, but the index is the middle of the frame — so the point picked (the raw data index used) is the middle one, but its stored value is overwritten with the minmax value. This distorts x-position? Actually the x dimension is retained from the original data at that raw index... wait, only the value dim is cloned. Actually `clone([dimension], true)` — target store only contains that dimension. But the SeriesData downSample keeps other dims via indices.

Let me look at the actual upstream fix. Upstream commit: "fix(sample): fix minmax sampling behaviour" — PR #19150? Let me recall: The upstream fix (commit c89632d, ECharts 5.5.1?) changed dataSample.ts: the minmax sampler to return index, and changed how sampleValue/sampleIndex interact. Actually the actual upstream fix:

```ts
minmax: function (frame) {
    let turningPointAbsoluteValue = -Infinity;
    let turningPointOriginalValue = -Infinity;

    for (let i = 0; i < frame.length; i++) {
        const originalValue = frame[i];
        const absoluteValue = Math.abs(originalValue);

        if (absoluteValue > turningPointAbsoluteValue) {
            turningPointAbsoluteValue = absoluteValue;
            turningPointOriginalValue = originalValue;
        }
    }

    return isFinite(turningPointOriginalValue) ? turningPointOriginalValue : NaN;
},
